    "abstract": {
      "en": "Extent of Intact Forest Landscapes (IFLs) in the Caucasus region in 2013. Intact Forest Landscapes are large, continuous areas of natural ecosystems that show no significant signs of human activity or habitat fragmentation. The dataset provides an updated assessment of forest integrity across the Caucasus and serves as a reference for evaluating changes in forest condition, biodiversity conservation, and ecosystem connectivity over time.",
