    "notes": {
      "en": "<ul><li>Intact Forest Landscapes (IFLs) are unfragmented natural ecosystems large enough to maintain native biodiversity and ecological processes.</li><li>The layer represents forest conditions in 2013.</li><li>IFL boundaries were derived from satellite imagery and ancillary environmental datasets.</li><li>The dataset supports assessments of forest integrity, habitat connectivity, and conservation planning.</li><li>This layer can be compared with the 2000 IFL dataset to identify areas of forest loss, fragmentation, or persistence.</li></ul>",
      "fr": "",
      "es": "",
      "ar": "",
